You saved the water for my people.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.140
Sir, the credit goes to Yasmin.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.920
I never could have done it without her help.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.640
Where did you learn to do such things?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.740
It is not a woman's place.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:06.400
Father, you would not teach me to run the well, but you could not stop me from watching

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:08.780
over your shoulder as you taught others.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:13.060
Perhaps it is time for a change in Alkaline.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:16.130
For many changes, Father.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:19.930
Oh, Daddy, we had the most amazing time!

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:22.470
We met a real sheikh and stayed in a palace.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.660
Yes, I'm sure it was most enlightening.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:30.000
In fact, I'd like you all to write a ten-page essay about your trip, due on Monday.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:36.100
Now I'm glad I didn't go on that silly trip.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.050
You weren't so happy about it a few days ago, Trevor.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.050
Really, Trevor? You're not being very nice.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:45.860
Especially considering we brought you back a gift from the desert.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:47.860
A gift? Really?

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:48.740
Let me have it.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.740
Alright, you asked for it.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:58.040
Sand?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.830
Really?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.620
Not at all nice, Mr. Bond.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.630
At least Trevor won't be hungry, sir.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:04.780
No, why not?

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:09.480
He can just dig into his pockets for the sandwiches there.
